{% comment %}
Stage 3 of the decider — the follow-ups to a step's coercion type, batched in one exchange. Stage 2 picked the type by
name; here, for a step whose option holds a type:
- KindOf (ruling 10): which kind the type carries — a number's int/long/double/decimal, an item's json, a text's
  md/xml, a duration's iso/short/dotnet — or, for a generic (list, dict), its element type, the types offered again.
  The answer combines with the picked type into {name, kind}; "none" keeps it bare.
- Strict: a yes/no — whether the step marks the coercion strict (the value must actually BE that type), setting the
  type's strict flag; asked for any type coercion, with or without a kind.
Only these render here; a build with none renders {} and the stage is skipped. The keys and wording are pinned by
PickListTests (PLang.Tests/Wire/App/Decider/pick_golden.json).
{% endcomment %}
{
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
{%- for s in goal.Step -%}
{%- assign text = s.Text -%}
{%- for q in s.Pick.Question -%}
{%- if q.Kind == "KindOf" -%}
{%- if q.Of == "list" or q.Of == "dict" -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. It coerces to a {{ q.Of }}. A {{ q.Of }} of what type — which type are its elements? Answer none if the step names no element type.{% endcapture -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. It coerces to `{{ q.Of }}`. Which kind of `{{ q.Of }}` does the step name? A word in the step beside the type word — one of the kinds offered here — names that kind; the type word and the kind word can sit together, in either order, or the kind word can stand alone as the coercion's target (`as <kind>`, `type=<kind>`): then it names its kind. None unless the step names one of these kinds; the type word alone (no kind word) names none.{% endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{ sep }}
  {{ q.Id | json }}: {
    "type": "choice",
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }},
    "criteria": {
{%- assign osep = "" -%}
{%- for v in q.Values -%}
{{ osep }}{{ v | json }}: null
{%- assign osep = ", " -%}
{%- endfor -%}
}
  }
{%- assign sep = "," -%}
{%- elsif q.Kind == "Strict" -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. It coerces to `{{ q.Of }}`. Is that coercion STRICT — does the step say the value must actually BE a `{{ q.Of }}`, so a mismatch is an error rather than a best-effort hint (the word "strict"/"strictly")? Answer yes only if the step marks it strict; otherwise no.{% endcapture -%}
{{ sep }}
  {{ q.Id | json }}: {
    "type": "noul",
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }}
  }
{%- assign sep = "," -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor %}
}
